#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# polynomial_extended_gcd

#% text
# `polynomial_extended_gcd(p, q, x)` gives `[g, [s, t]]`: the monic greatest common divisor `g` of `p` and `q` and polynomials with `g = s p + t q`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
polynomial_extended_gcd(x^2 - 1, x^3 - 1, x)
#% output
#= [-1 + x, [-x, 1]]

#% cell
polynomial_extended_gcd(x^2 + 1, x^3 + x + 1, x)
#% output
#= [1, [-x, 1]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `polynomial_gcd`, `extended_gcd`
